The report templates, the HTML/widget presentation layer, the native SVG chart
renderer, the configuration model and the type-inference framework come from
that project. The statistics engine was rewritten on Polars LazyFrames, and the
pandas and Spark backends were removed.

The type-inference design (a tree of identity relations plus inference
relations walked from a generic root type) follows visions
(https://github.com/dylan-profiler/visions) by Ian Eaves and Simon Brugman.

The augmented Dickey-Fuller p-values use the response-surface regression
coefficients of MacKinnon (1994, 2010), as published in statsmodels
(BSD-3-Clause, https://github.com/statsmodels/statsmodels).

